Z||000017||fiero56||12-14-1999||09:30 AM||||Even if it is 30-40mpg, I'd say that is pretty good, especially durring the time period the car was made, 1984.||||reg||1
Z||000018||william_thorniii||12-15-1999||09:47 PM||||The reason that the gas gage is always moving while the car is accelerating/decelerating or going up/down hills is because of the shape of the tank more than anything else.  Since our tank runs through the center console of the vehicle it is very narrow and long from front to back.  This design was created for cornering, to keep the car with an even right and left hand side weight.  Normal cars have a shallow tank that is long from side to side, but the concern was that in cornering this slosh of fuel can sometimes carry enough momentum to throw the balance of the vehicle.  Hence our long (front to back) tanks.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
